.TH MDPURGE 1 "2026-09-17" "emerald" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mdpurge \- remove unused build dependencies
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mdpurge
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ package ... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mdpurge
removes installed build dependencies that are no longer required by the installed package set. Without package arguments, all eligible build dependencies are considered. With package arguments, only the specified packages are considered.
.PP
The command checks the package dependency graph before removal and does not remove packages required at runtime or listed in the world file. Build dependencies are not retained; they are installed again automatically when a package is rebuilt.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -n, --dryrun
Print packages that would be removed without removing them.
.TP
.B -y, --yes
Remove packages without confirmation.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show help.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
mdpurge --dryrun
mdpurge --yes
mdpurge --dryrun cmake ninja
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success; non-zero on invalid options, failed verification, cancellation, or removal failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR emerald (1),
.BR pkgdel (1)
